english_question:
As shown in the figure, the correct conclusions are ______ (select all the correct conclusion numbers) 
(1) If \(AB \parallel CD\), then \(∠3 = ∠4\); 
(2) If \(∠1 = ∠BEG\), then \(EF \parallel GH\); 
(3) If \(∠FGH + ∠3 = 180^{\circ}\), then \(EF \parallel GH\); 
(4) If \(AB \parallel CD\), \(∠4 = 62^{\circ}\), and \(EG\) bisects \(∠BEF\), then \(∠1 = 59^{\circ}\).

In the figure, $AC$ is the diagonal of rhombus $ABCD$, and $AE = EF = FC$. Then, $\boldsymbol{S}_{\triangle BMN} : \boldsymbol{S}_{\text{rhombus } ABCD} = ( )
A. \frac{3}{4}
B. \frac{3}{7}
C. \frac{3}{8}
D. \frac{3}{10}

Given the front view and top view of a triangular pyramid as shown in the figure, what is the area of the side view of the triangular pyramid? ( )
A. \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
B. \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4}
C. 1
D. \frac{1}{2}

In the figure, given triangle ABC where AB = BC, a circle with diameter AB intersects AC at point D. The tangent line from point D to circle O intersects BC at point E. If CD = 5 and CE = 4, what is the radius of circle O?
A. 3
B. 4
C. \frac{25}{6}
D. \frac{25}{8}

In the figure, line l is perpendicular to plane α, with foot O. The edge length of the regular tetrahedron ABCD is 8, C is in plane α, and B is a moving point on line l. When the distance from O to AD is maximized, the projected area of the regular tetrahedron on plane α is ( )
A. 4 + 2 \sqrt{2}
B. 16 + 8 \sqrt{2}
C. 8 + 8 \sqrt{2}
D. 16
